- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sum queries
- Maintaining a running best to optimize transitions from O(n) to O(1)
- Reconstruction of exact intervals

## DP Recurrence
Let pref[i] = sum of first i elements (pref[0] = 0).

**Transition:**
dp[i][t] = max(
  dp[i-1][t],                                    // Don't end a subarray at i
  best[t] + pref[i]                              // End a subarray at i
)

where best[t] = max_{1 ≤ l ≤ i} (dp[l-1][t-1] - pref[l-1])

**Initialization:**
dp[0][0] = 0, dp[0][t>0] = -∞

**Answer:** dp[n][k]

## Reconstruction
Track which choice was made at each dp[i][t]. If dp[i][t] came from dp[i-1][t], no subarray ends at i. Otherwise, find l where dp[l-1][t-1] - pref[l-1] = best[t], and record subarray (l..i).

## Complexity
- Time: O(nk) with O(1) transitions using running best
- Space: O(nk) for dp table, O(nk) for reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = [0];
  for (let x of A) pref.push(pref[pref.length - 1] + x);

  const dp = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(-Infinity));
  const choice = Array.from({ length: n + 1 }, () => Array(k + 1).fill(0));
  dp[0][0] = 0;

  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      // Skip position i
      if (dp[i - 1][t] >= dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = dp[i - 1][t];
        choice[i][t] = 0; // 0 = skip
      }

      // Start/extend subarray ending at i
      if (t > 0) {
        let best = -Infinity;
        for (let l = 1; l <= i; l++) {
          const val = dp[l - 1][t - 1] + (pref[i] - pref[l - 1]) - c;
          if (val > best) best = val;
        }
        if (best > dp[i][t]) {
          dp[i][t] = best;
          choice[i][t] = 1; // 1 = take subarray ending at i
        }
      }
    }
  }

  // Reconstruction
  const subarrays = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (i > 0 && t > 0) {
    if (choice[i][t] === 1) {
      let l = 1;
      for (let j = 1; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j - 1][t - 1] + (pref[i] - pref[j - 1]) - c;
        if (val === dp[i][t]) {
          l = j;
          break;
        }
      }
      subarrays.unshift([l - 1, i - 1]); // Convert to 0-indexed
      t--;
    }
    i--;
  }

  return { value: dp[n][k], subarrays };
}
```

## Optimized O(nk) Version
The inner loop can be optimized by maintaining a running best:
```javascript
for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
  for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
    best[t] = Math.max(best[t], dp[i - 1][t - 1] - pref[i - 1]);
    dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i - 1][t], best[t] + pref[i] - c);
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP state augmentation for a path with a constrained number of turns, combining path optimization with reconstruction. It demands careful handling of transitions when direction changes. 

## Key Concepts
- DP on grid paths with turn constraints
- 4D state dp[i][j][t][dir]
- Reconstruction via parent pointers
- Time: O(n*m*k); Space: O(n*m*k)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxPathWithKTurns(grid, K) {
  const n = grid.length, m = grid[0].length;
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n}, () =>
    Array.from({length: m}, () => Array.from({length: K+1}, () => [NEG, NEG]))
  );
  dp[0][0][0][0] = grid[0][0];
  dp[0][0][0][1] = grid[0][0];
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let j = 0; j < m; j++) {
      if (i === 0 && j === 0) continue;
      for (let t = 0; t <= K; t++) {
        const val = grid[i][j];
        if (j > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][0], dp[i][j-1][t][0] + val);
          if (t > 0) dp[i][j][t][0] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][0], dp[i][j-1][t-1][1] + val);
        }
        if (i > 0) {
          dp[i][j][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][1], dp[i-1][j][t][1] + val);
          if (t > 0) dp[i][j][t][1] = Math.max(dp[i][j][t][1], dp[i-1][j][t-1][0] + val);
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction would backtrack using stored choices (omitted for brevity)
  return {dp, best: Math.max(...Array.from({length:K+1}, (_,t)=>Math.max(dp[n-1][m-1][t][0], dp[n-1][m-1][t][1])))};
}
```
